WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/MoreDetailsPanel.tsx — a PURE presentational panel that takes
  `drive: DriveDetail` + `stats: DriveStats` (already converted to the user's display units by the parent
  `useDriveDetailData` hook per ADR-004) and renders, inside FadeIn → GlassPanel(p-5):
    header  : <Activity/> icon (cyan) + "More Details"
    grid #1 : Odometer(cyan) · Range(green) · Elevation(green ↑ / red ↓) · Energy Consumed(amber)
              · Energy Recovered(green) · Consumption(purple)
    grid #2 : Avg Power(amber) · [Avg Outside Temp(blue)] · [Avg Inside Temp(orange)] · Min Speed(secondary)
              · Battery Used(amber) · Net Consumption(cyan)        (the two temp tiles are conditional: !== null)
  The ONLY conversion the panel itself does is `toEfficiencyDisplay` (Wh/km → Wh/mi when distance unit is miles)
  + the `efficiencyUnit` label. Number formatting is `fmtNumber` (global precision, default 2) / `fmtInt` (0 dp);
  Battery Used is a raw `${startPct - endPct}%` integer subtraction; energy uses the `>1000 ? kWh : Wh` threshold.
  Rendering nuances reproduced exactly: unit muted-and-separate (Odometer/Range/Consumption/Avg Power) vs.
  embedded-in-colored-value (Energy*/Net/Temps) vs. value+unit both secondary (Min Speed) vs. the two-line
  green/red elevation block.  useUnits is the only "data source"; there are no charts and no maps.

